{"cid:135449284":{"key":"cid:135449284","title":"Inosine pranobex","compound":{"key":"cid:135449284","cid":135449284,"qid":"Q3130053","title":"Inosine Pranobex","iupac":"tris(4-acetamidobenzoic acid);9-[(2R,3R,4S,5R)-3,4-dihydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)oxolan-2-yl]-1H-purin-6-one;tris(1-(dimethylamino)propan-2-ol)","wiki_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inosine_pranobex","cas":"36703-88-5","iuphar":null,"drugbank":"DB13156","chemspider":"34411","unii":"W1SO0V223F","kegg":"D01995","chebi":null,"chembl":null,"pdb_ligand":null,"comptox":null,"echa":"100.048.313","description":"mixture of chemical compounds","kind":null,"atc":"J05AX05","mesh":"D007542","uniprot":null,"ncbi_taxon":null,"gbif":null,"powo":null,"extra_at":"2026-11-08T19:46:41+00:00","eml":null,"smiles":"CC(CN(C)C)O.CC(CN(C)C)O.CC(CN(C)C)O.CC(=O)NC1=CC=C(C=C1)C(=O)O.CC(=O)NC1=CC=C(C=C1)C(=O)O.CC(=O)NC1=CC=C(C=C1)C(=O)O.C1=NC2=C(C(=O)N1)N=CN2[C@H]3[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H](O3)CO)O)O","chembl_phase":null,"first_approval":null,"bbw":null,"fda":0,"ema":1,"control":null,"reg_at":"2026-11-10T10:49:37+00:00"},"status":null,"pharm":[{"section":"Drug Indication","items":[{"section":"Drug Indication","text":"Inosine pranobex is also indicated for mucocutaneous infections due to herpes simplex virus (type 1 and type II) and for treatment of genital warts as adjunctive therapy to podophyllin or carbon dioxide laser.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13156","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"MeSH Pharmacological Classification","items":[{"section":"MeSH Pharmacological Classification","text":"Substances that augment, stimulate, activate, potentiate, or modulate the immune response at either the cellular or humoral level. The classical agents (Freund&apos;s adjuvant, BCG, Corynebacterium parvum, et al.) contain bacterial antigens. Some are endogenous (e.g., histamine, interferon, transfer factor, tuftsin, interleukin-1). Their mode of action is either non-specific, resulting in increased immune responsiveness to a wide variety of antigens, or antigen-specific, i.e., affecting a restricted type of immune response to a narrow group of antigens. The therapeutic efficacy of many biological response modifiers is related to their antigen-specific immunoadjuvanticity.","source":"Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)","url":"https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/M0000431.html","license_url":"https://www.nlm.nih.gov/copyright.html"},{"section":"MeSH Pharmacological Classification","text":"Agents used in the prophylaxis or therapy of VIRUS DISEASES. Some of the ways they may act include preventing viral replication by inhibiting viral DNA polymerase; binding to specific cell-surface receptors and inhibiting viral penetration or uncoating; inhibiting viral protein synthesis; or blocking late stages of virus assembly.","source":"Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)","url":"https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/M0001518.html","license_url":"https://www.nlm.nih.gov/copyright.html"}]},{"section":"Pharmacodynamics","items":[{"section":"Pharmacodynamics","text":"Works by slowing the growth and spread of the virus in the body. It may also stimulate the immune system in the body, which helps to increase the body's ability to fight these infections.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13156","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Mechanism of Action","items":[{"section":"Mechanism of Action","text":"Inosine pranobex stimulates cell-mediated immune processes to viral infections.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13156","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","items":[{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","text":"Rapidly absorbed from GIT","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13156","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"},{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","text":"Via urine","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13156","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Biological Half-Life","items":[{"section":"Biological Half-Life","text":"50 min","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13156","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]}],"safety":[],"manufacturing":[],"structure":true,"populations":{"child":{"label":"Suitable for children","count":2,"forms":[["Oral Syrup",1],["Syrup",1]]},"noswallow":{"label":"No tablet or capsule to swallow","count":2,"forms":[["Oral Syrup",1],["Syrup",1]]}},"reg":{"fda":0,"ema":1,"phase":null,"first_approval":null,"bbw":false,"control":null,"withdrawn":[],"reg_checked":true,"aware":null},"chem":{"props":{"key":"cid:135449284","title":"Inosine pranobex","products":3,"mw":268.2,"logp":-2.27,"tpsa":133.5,"hbd":4,"hba":7,"rotb":2,"rings":3,"heavy":19,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C10H12N4O5"},"similar":[{"key":"cid:9444","title":"Azacitidine","products":5,"mw":244.2,"logp":-3.17,"tpsa":143.7,"hbd":4,"hba":8,"rotb":2,"rings":2,"heavy":17,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C8H12N4O5","similarity":0.56},{"key":"cid:6253","title":"Cytarabine","products":6,"mw":243.2,"logp":-2.56,"tpsa":130.8,"hbd":4,"hba":7,"rotb":2,"rings":2,"heavy":17,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C9H13N3O5","similarity":0.472},{"key":"cid:6083","title":"Adenosine monophosphate","products":1,"mw":347.2,"logp":-1.86,"tpsa":186.1,"hbd":5,"hba":9,"rotb":4,"rings":3,"heavy":23,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C10H14N5O7P","similarity":0.467},{"key":"cid:6029","title":"Uridine","products":1,"mw":244.2,"logp":-2.85,"tpsa":124.8,"hbd":4,"hba":6,"rotb":2,"rings":2,"heavy":17,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C9H12N2O6","similarity":0.462},{"key":"cid:5957","title":"Adenosine triphosphate","products":3,"mw":507.2,"logp":-1.63,"tpsa":279.1,"hbd":7,"hba":13,"rotb":8,"rings":3,"heavy":31,"lipinski":3,"formula":"C10H16N5O13P3","similarity":0.431},{"key":"cid:30751","title":"Fludarabine","